// Round 8: `sword_drawn: true` added. A fresh level leaves the right hand empty on the original, so the press
// at tick 5 only drew the sword and the earlier capture never swung (the dummy kept 50 health); with the
// sword given and its draw run out first, the press attacks. The port starts with the sword in hand.
// Sword sweep width, one point of the sweep over lateral offset (60 / 90 uu to the side of the view
// line, 140 uu ahead). m_fSweepingAttackSize is 60 (half 30) and the pawn radius 35, so the
// design reading is a hit within about 65 uu: UNMEASURED. The port uses the same bound.
(
    name: "combat/melee_lateral_90",
    system: Combat,
    map: "Playground",
    description: "One swing at a passive guard 140 uu ahead and 90 uu to the side.",
    setup: (
        player: Some((sword_drawn: true, position: (-5300, 0, 96), yaw: 180, pitch: -5)),
        npcs: [(id: Some("dummy"), position: Some((-5440, 90, 92)), yaw: 0, state: Some("Passive"))],
        settle: 30,
    ),
    ticks: 120,
    input: [(tick: 5, action: Press(Primary))],
    checkpoints: [
        (name: "connects", expect: [(metric: Count("Sim:Damage@dummy"), value: 0, tol: 0, source: "sweep width 60 + radius 35 (melee.md)", status: Unmeasured)]),
    ],
    record: [Pawn, Npc("dummy"), SimEvents],
    capture: Some("measure sword npc=<placed guard> --swings 1 at lateral offset 90"),
)